  <title>2.6.2: Writing a New System to Solve a Given System</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00460</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.6.2: Writing a New System to Solve a Given System</md:title>
    <md:uuid>320a5da8-da02-4ce6-ab08-543a0177df6b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Here is a system you solved by graphing earlier.</para>
<para>\( \begin {cases}\begin {align} 4x + \hspace{2.2mm} y &amp;= \hspace {2mm}1 &amp;\quad&amp;\text{Equation A}\\ x + 2y &amp;= \hspace {2mm} 9&amp;\quad&amp;\text{Equation B} \end{align} \end{cases} \)</para>
<para>To start solving the system, Elena wrote:</para>
<para>\( \begin {align} 4x + \hspace{2.2mm} y &amp;= \hspace {2mm}1\\ 4x + 8y &amp;= 36 \end{align} \)</para>
<para>And then she wrote:</para>
<para>\( \begin {align} 4x + \hspace{2.2mm} y &amp;= \hspace {3mm}1\\-(4x + 8y &amp;= \hspace{1mm}36 ) \hspace{1.5mm} \\ \overline {\hspace{8mm}\text-7y} &amp;\overline{\hspace{1mm}=\text-35 \hspace{5mm}}\end{align} \)</para>
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What was Elena’s first move?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> First, she multiplied each side of the second equation by 4, which produces an equivalent equation with \(4x\) in it.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q2-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What was Elena’s second move?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Next, she subtracted the new equation from the first equation. Doing that creates another equation where the variable \(x\) is eliminated, leaving only one variable and making it possible to solve for \(y\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q3-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What might be possible reasons for those moves?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Doing these steps creates another equation where the \(x\) variable is eliminated, leaving only one variable making it possible to solve for \(y\). </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q4-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Complete the solving process algebraically. Show that the solution is indeed \(x=-1\), \(y=5\).</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\( -7y=-35 \) can be rewritten as \(y=5\). Substituting 5 for \(y\) in the first equation, we have \(4x+5=1\) or \(4x=-4\), which means \(x=-1\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
